          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Impact on Art and Culture</strong><br>\nThe Polaroid camera had a significant impact on art and culture. Artists were drawn to the immediacy and uniqueness of Polaroid pictures. This new form of photography was used for artistic expression, and Land's work influenced a generation of photographers and artists, who embraced the new creative possibilities.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Vision for the Future</strong><br>\nEdwin Land was a visionary who believed in the power of innovation. He often spoke about the importance of scientific research and development. Land's work at Polaroid included ventures into 3D movies and the Polavision instant movie camera, reflecting his constant push for technological advancement.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nEdwin Land passed away in 1991, but his legacy lives on. The Polaroid camera remains a beloved piece of technology, symbolizing innovation and the joy of photography. Land's contribution to optics and photography continues to be recognized as fundamental to the field, and his spirit of invention inspires new generations of scientists and inventors.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
